#X text 394 62 Slicer4 is a stereo sampler engine primarily useful for breakbeats. The original tempo of the sample is calculated based on the assumption that it's a 4/4 meter (and either 1 \, 2 or 4 bars in length). BPM can be adjusted \, e.g. to the global tempo of the main patch. The sample can be split 0-5 times resulting in 1-32 equal slices that are played back in a randomly generated but fixed pattern (mode 0) or a totally random order (mode 1). Inject preset patterns through the second inlet \, abstraction presets through third. Fourth inlet allows overriding slice order and duration by another instance of Slicer4., f 46;
